## Mod

This application uses `tey/mod` for file placement and discovery. Before placing a file, run `php artisan mod:list --json` or `mod-inventory` and read the active layout, file types, templates and scaffolds. Prefer the matching `mod:*` generator with explicit placement. Preview with `--dry-run --json`; inspect files, warnings and `would_write` before writing. Load `mod-development` for options and the package API.

Call `mod-survey` without arguments for structure, references and recurring sets. Call `mod-fit` with an uninstalled layout or recipe manifest for ownership, conflicts, variances, outside touches and code configuration. Both read only `base_path()` (plus local Git metadata for survey), classify vendor references, exclude secrets/runtime data and symlinks, and make no writes or network calls. The skill documents inputs, privacy and limits. Load `mod-learning-patterns` to learn this app's conventions and propose a layout and scaffold recipes for human review, checking them with `mod-fit`. Never adopt proposals automatically.
